From 8442ecfaca997060d8d3007f96461da0481b7799 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Van Tran <trantoanvan@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:52:57 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(triage): suggest a new issue's project and Type with a
 fast decision model
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cloudflare Workers AI's Clef (Jev's "System One" shape: choice questions,
calibrated probabilities) answers in about 200 ms. Learned from OpenMausBot's
decider: fail open (no key, timeout 1.5 s, HTTP error or an answer that does
not validate = no suggestion), the top option's probability must reach 0.6,
and the log line holds the choice, probability, margin, latency and a state
hash, never the issue text or the token. From Linear's Triage Intelligence:
project and team-like fields, workspace history as context, the workspace's
own guidance, auto-apply only where chosen.

Everything offered is read from the workspace on every call: projects (name,
description, recent issue titles) and the property the workflow rules use,
else one named Type (its options, its description as guidance, recent issues
per option). Nothing about options is built in.

- POST /api/issues/triage-suggest {title, description, project_id, has_type}
  returns only the fields the model is sure of (often none).
- A chat /issue (origin *_chat) with no project gets project and Type when
  sure, plus a line "_Clef xếp: <project> 87% · <Type> 91%_"; any refusal
  creates the issue as typed.
- MULTICA_WORKERS_AI_ACCOUNT_ID + MULTICA_WORKERS_AI_TOKEN turn it on;
  MULTICA_TRIAGE_FORM=off / MULTICA_TRIAGE_CHAT=off switch a job off.
- Opt-in live eval (TRIAGE_LIVE_EVAL=1) against a workspace's issues or a
  fixture of requests.

Patch-Id: triage-suggest
